>> servings: 8
>> tags: Baking, Dessert

== Pastry ==

Rub the @butter{100%g} into the flour, @icing sugar{50%g} and @salt{=1%pinch} until it looks like breadcrumbs. Add the yolk and enough water to bring it together. @plain flour{200%g} @egg yolk{1} @cold water{1%tbsp}

Wrap and chill ~{30%minutes}. Roll out to line a 23 cm tart tin, trim, and chill again.

Blind bake at 180°C for ~{20%minutes} with baking paper and weights, then ~{5%minutes} without, until pale gold.

== Filling ==

Turn the oven down to 150°C.

Whisk the @egg{4} and sugar until just combined, then whisk in the @lemon juice{150%ml}, zest and cream. @caster sugar{150%g} @thickened cream{150%ml}

Pour into the warm pastry case and bake ~{25%minutes}, until set at the edges with a slight wobble in the centre.

== To finish ==

Cool completely in the tin, then chill at least ~{2%hours}.

Dust with icing sugar and serve with cream. @double cream{150%ml}
